{
  "captured_at": "2026-10-23T20:13:11.089Z",
  "status": "Source-view lines captured unchanged while scrolling to bottom; byte identity not established",
  "lines": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "\"\"\"Paid local-transition execution of a learned martingale control."
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "No conditional expectation, transition matrix, value function, normalizer,"
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "or learned-domain membership oracle is an input. The caller supplies a frozen"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "bounded potential h, a bounded terminal payoff, and genuinely fresh transition"
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "forks from saved full states. A fixed finite horizon bounds source calls."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "line": 7,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "line": 8,
      "text": "Exact rational implementation for auditing. This is a control-variate and"
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "line": 9,
      "text": "Horvitz--Thompson construction; historical priority of this specialization is"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "line": 10,
      "text": "UNKNOWN. Strong retaining methods are entitled to every operation here."
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "line": 11,
      "text": "\"\"\""
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "line": 12,
      "text": "from dataclasses import dataclass"
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "line": 13,
      "text": "from fractions import Fraction as F"
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "line": 14,
      "text": "import random"
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "line": 15,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "line": 16,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "line": 17,
      "text": "def rational(x):"
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "line": 18,
      "text": "    if type(x) is F:"
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "line": 19,
      "text": "        return x"
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "line": 20,
      "text": "    if type(x) is int:"
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "line": 21,
      "text": "        return F(x)"
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "line": 22,
      "text": "    raise TypeError(\"Exact int or Fraction required\")"
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "line": 23,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "line": 24,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "line": 25,
      "text": "def bounded(x):"
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "line": 26,
      "text": "    x = rational(x)"
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "line": 27,
      "text": "    if not 0 <= x <= 1:"
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "line": 28,
      "text": "        raise ValueError(\"Observable must be in [0,1]\")"
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "line": 29,
      "text": "    return x"
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "line": 30,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "line": 31,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "line": 32,
      "text": "@dataclass(frozen=True)"
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "line": 33,
      "text": "class Plan:"
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "line": 34,
      "text": "    horizon: int"
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "line": 35,
      "text": "    probes: int"
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "line": 36,
      "text": "    beta: F = F(1)"
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "line": 37,
      "text": "    gamma: F = F(0)"
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "line": 38,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "line": 39,
      "text": "    def __post_init__(self):"
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "line": 40,
      "text": "        if type(self.horizon) is not int or self.horizon < 1:"
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "line": 41,
      "text": "            raise ValueError(\"Positive integer horizon required\")"
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "line": 42,
      "text": "        if type(self.probes) is not int or self.probes < 1:"
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "line": 43,
      "text": "            raise ValueError(\"Positive integer probe count required\")"
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "line": 44,
      "text": "        if type(self.beta) is not F or type(self.gamma) is not F:"
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "line": 45,
      "text": "            raise TypeError(\"Coefficients must be exact Fractions\")"
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "line": 46,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "line": 47,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "line": 48,
      "text": "class ChargedRandom:"
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "line": 49,
      "text": "    \"\"\"Exact categorical sampling with observed, not hard-capped, bit cost."
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "line": 50,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "line": 51,
      "text": "    Rejection sampling can use arbitrarily many bits; its actual consumption"
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "line": 52,
      "text": "    and rejected words are retained. Expected words per nontrivial draw < 2."
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "line": 53,
      "text": "    This Python seeded PRNG is an executable fixture, not physical entropy."
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "line": 54,
      "text": "    \"\"\""
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "line": 55,
      "text": "    def __init__(self, seed):"
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "line": 56,
      "text": "        if type(seed) is not int:"
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "line": 57,
      "text": "            raise TypeError(\"Integer seed required\")"
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "line": 58,
      "text": "        self.generator = random.Random(seed)"
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "line": 59,
      "text": "        self.bits = 0"
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "line": 60,
      "text": "        self.words = []"
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "line": 61,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "line": 62,
      "text": "    def below(self, n):"
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "line": 63,
      "text": "        if type(n) is not int or n < 1:"
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "line": 64,
      "text": "            raise ValueError(\"Positive integer bound required\")"
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "line": 65,
      "text": "        if n == 1:"
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "line": 66,
      "text": "            return 0"
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "line": 67,
      "text": "        width = (n - 1).bit_length()"
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "line": 68,
      "text": "        while True:"
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "line": 69,
      "text": "            word = self.generator.getrandbits(width)"
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "line": 70,
      "text": "            self.bits += width"
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "line": 71,
      "text": "            self.words.append((width, word, n, word < n))"
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "line": 72,
      "text": "            if word < n:"
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "line": 73,
      "text": "                return word"
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "line": 74,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "line": 75,
      "text": "    def categorical(self, weights):"
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "line": 76,
      "text": "        weights = tuple(weights)"
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "line": 77,
      "text": "        if not weights or any(type(w) is not int or w < 0 for w in weights):"
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "line": 78,
      "text": "            raise ValueError(\"Nonnegative integer weights required\")"
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "line": 79,
      "text": "        total = sum(weights)"
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "line": 80,
      "text": "        if total < 1:"
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "line": 81,
      "text": "            raise ValueError(\"A positive total weight is required\")"
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "line": 82,
      "text": "        z = self.below(total)"
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "line": 83,
      "text": "        for i, weight in enumerate(weights):"
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "line": 84,
      "text": "            if z < weight:"
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "line": 85,
      "text": "                return i"
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "line": 86,
      "text": "            z -= weight"
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "line": 87,
      "text": "        raise AssertionError(\"Unreachable categorical endpoint\")"
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "line": 88,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "line": 89,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "line": 90,
      "text": "def validate_weights(weights, length):"
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "line": 91,
      "text": "    weights = tuple(weights)"
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "line": 92,
      "text": "    if len(weights) != length or any(type(w) is not int or w <= 0 for w in weights):"
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "line": 93,
      "text": "        raise ValueError(\"One strictly positive integer weight per path position required\")"
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "line": 94,
      "text": "    return weights"
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "line": 95,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "line": 96,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "line": 97,
      "text": "def estimate(start, step, is_terminal, potential, payoff, score, plan, rng):"
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "line": 98,
      "text": "    \"\"\"Return terminal estimate plus two exact, mean-zero learned controls."
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "line": 99,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "line": 100,
      "text": "    step(state,time,role) returns one next full state; fresh side calls must be"
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "line": 101,
      "text": "    independent conditional on the complete retained main path. Source-state"
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "line": 102,
      "text": "    serialization/restoration and source randomness are caller costs."
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "line": 103,
      "text": "    potential(time,state) and payoff(time,state) are frozen functions in [0,1]."
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "line": 104,
      "text": "    score(states,h_values) returns positive integer weights for ALL preterminal"
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "line": 105,
      "text": "    positions. It may inspect the full main path, but no fresh side outcome."
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "line": 106,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "line": 107,
      "text": "    Q = payoff_T - h_T + h_0 + mean(side_increment / rho_I)."
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "line": 108,
      "text": "    J = mean(main_increment / rho_I - (h_T - h_0))."
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "line": 109,
      "text": "    answer = payoff_T + beta*(Q-payoff_T) - gamma*J."
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "line": 110,
      "text": "    Any fixed beta,gamma preserve expectation. Training them on this same"
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "line": 111,
      "text": "    realization does not satisfy this interface."
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "line": 112,
      "text": "    \"\"\""
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "line": 113,
      "text": "    if type(plan) is not Plan or type(rng) is not ChargedRandom:"
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "line": 114,
      "text": "        raise TypeError(\"Validated Plan and ChargedRandom required\")"
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "line": 115,
      "text": "    # Reconstruct to reject a dataclass changed through object.__setattr__."
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "line": 116,
      "text": "    Plan(plan.horizon, plan.probes, plan.beta, plan.gamma)"
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "line": 117,
      "text": "    states = [start]"
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "line": 118,
      "text": "    for time in range(plan.horizon):"
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "line": 119,
      "text": "        if is_terminal(states[-1]):"
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "line": 120,
      "text": "            break"
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "line": 121,
      "text": "        states.append(step(states[-1], time, \"main\"))"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "line": 122,
      "text": "    length = len(states) - 1"
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "line": 123,
      "text": "    hs = tuple(bounded(potential(t, x)) for t, x in enumerate(states))"
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "line": 124,
      "text": "    target_sample = bounded(payoff(length, states[-1]))"
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "line": 125,
      "text": "    if length == 0:"
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "line": 126,
      "text": "        return {\"states\": tuple(states), \"h\": hs, \"weights\": (),"
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "line": 127,
      "text": "                \"terminal\": target_sample, \"quadrature\": target_sample,"
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "line": 128,
      "text": "                \"index_control\": F(0), \"estimate\": target_sample,"
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "line": 129,
      "text": "                \"main_calls\": 0, \"side_calls\": 0, \"h_calls\": 1,"
    },
    {
      "index": 129,
      "line": 130,
      "text": "                \"payoff_calls\": 1, \"probe_tape\": (), \"index_bits\": 0,"
    },
    {
      "index": 130,
      "line": 131,
      "text": "                \"path_weight_ratio\": F(0)}"
    },
    {
      "index": 131,
      "line": 132,
      "text": "    weights = validate_weights(score(tuple(states), hs), length)"
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "line": 133,
      "text": "    total = sum(weights)"
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "line": 134,
      "text": "    main_change = hs[-1] - hs[0]"
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "line": 135,
      "text": "    probes = []"
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "line": 136,
      "text": "    ds, js = F(0), F(0)"
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "line": 137,
      "text": "    bits_before = rng.bits"
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "line": 138,
      "text": "    for _ in range(plan.probes):"
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "line": 139,
      "text": "        index = rng.categorical(weights)"
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "line": 140,
      "text": "        rho = F(weights[index], total)"
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "line": 141,
      "text": "        child = step(states[index], index, \"side\")"
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "line": 142,
      "text": "        child_h = bounded(potential(index + 1, child))"
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "line": 143,
      "text": "        delta = child_h - hs[index]"
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "line": 144,
      "text": "        main_delta = hs[index + 1] - hs[index]"
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "line": 145,
      "text": "        d = delta / rho"
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "line": 146,
      "text": "        j = main_delta / rho - main_change"
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "line": 147,
      "text": "        ds += d"
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "line": 148,
      "text": "        js += j"
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "line": 149,
      "text": "        probes.append({\"index\": index, \"child\": child, \"child_h\": child_h,"
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "line": 150,
      "text": "                       \"rho\": rho, \"drift_sample\": d, \"index_control\": j})"
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "line": 151,
      "text": "    q = target_sample - hs[-1] + hs[0] + ds / plan.probes"
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "line": 152,
      "text": "    j = js / plan.probes"
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "line": 153,
      "text": "    answer = target_sample + plan.beta * (q - target_sample) - plan.gamma * j"
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "line": 154,
      "text": "    return {\"states\": tuple(states), \"h\": hs, \"weights\": weights,"
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "line": 155,
      "text": "            \"terminal\": target_sample, \"quadrature\": q, \"index_control\": j,"
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "line": 156,
      "text": "            \"estimate\": answer, \"main_calls\": length,"
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "line": 157,
      "text": "            \"side_calls\": plan.probes, \"h_calls\": length + 1 + plan.probes,"
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "line": 158,
      "text": "            \"payoff_calls\": 1, \"probe_tape\": tuple(probes),"
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "line": 159,
      "text": "            \"index_bits\": rng.bits - bits_before,"
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "line": 160,
      "text": "            \"path_weight_ratio\": F(total, min(weights))}"
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "line": 161,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "line": 162,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "line": 163,
      "text": "def output_range(weight_ratio_bound, beta, gamma):"
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "line": 164,
      "text": "    \"\"\"Deterministic enclosing interval from a GLOBAL declared rho bound."
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "line": 165,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "line": 166,
      "text": "    A data-dependent observed path ratio is insufficient for a confidence"
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "line": 167,
      "text": "    bound over unseen paths. A score=(1-eta)*learned+eta*uniform gives H/eta."
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "line": 168,
      "text": "    The returned enclosure supports ordinary bounded-mean inference; no"
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "line": 169,
      "text": "    claim that its conservative width is practically small is made."
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "line": 170,
      "text": "    \"\"\""
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "line": 171,
      "text": "    M, beta, gamma = map(rational, (weight_ratio_bound, beta, gamma))"
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "line": 172,
      "text": "    if M < 1:"
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "line": 173,
      "text": "        raise ValueError(\"Global inverse-probability bound must be at least 1\")"
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "line": 174,
      "text": "    radius = abs(beta) * (M + 1) + abs(gamma) * (M + 1)"
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "line": 175,
      "text": "    return -radius, 1 + radius"
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "line": 176,
      "text": "\n"
    }
  ],
